WEBVTT

00:18.560 --> 00:20.270
Damn it.

00:20.353 --> 00:21.521
CHOI TAE-HO

00:34.284 --> 00:38.163
MR. OH, HWANG YANG-JUNG
LEE DU-YEONG, HYEON-JU

00:46.713 --> 00:47.714
Aren't you going home?

00:48.214 --> 00:50.050
I was looking for a house, sir.

00:50.842 --> 00:53.678
Jeez. It's not easy
finding a home nowadays.

00:54.387 --> 00:55.805
What about your honeymoon?

00:56.389 --> 01:00.060
My wife wants to go to Paris,
but I don't think we can go due to COVID.

01:00.143 --> 01:01.936
Jeez. That damn COVID.

01:06.191 --> 01:07.859
What brings you here at this hour?

01:11.696 --> 01:12.530
Hey.

01:13.615 --> 01:14.783
There's a big case.

01:15.283 --> 01:18.453
I've been watching
a loan shark for about six months,

01:18.536 --> 01:22.373
and this bastard takes videos
of people to threaten them with.

01:22.874 --> 01:27.504
I got my hands on
a list of the bastard's victims today.

01:28.213 --> 01:32.050
I'll share the data with you.
Let's dive into it together.

01:34.010 --> 01:34.844
Yes, sir.

01:36.679 --> 01:37.931
- Get back to it.
- Yes, sir.

01:43.144 --> 01:43.978
Yes.

01:44.062 --> 01:46.272
He said he received the list today.

01:46.940 --> 01:48.775
He probably didn't do it alone.

01:49.400 --> 01:53.071
Find out who took part in it,
and I'll pay you 100 million per person.

01:53.822 --> 01:54.948
Yes, sir.

01:55.532 --> 01:57.659
When will you get Oh In-muk's location?

01:57.742 --> 02:02.038
I should be able to get the locations
of where he used his credit card

02:02.914 --> 02:05.208
in the last seven days
by tomorrow morning.

02:06.417 --> 02:08.837
I'll wire you the money
once I receive it. Good luck.

02:14.134 --> 02:15.093
A hundred million.

02:17.595 --> 02:18.638
How's it going?

02:20.431 --> 02:23.560
Only Jang-do knew
the location of the hard drive.

02:23.643 --> 02:26.563
The punk blurted it out
when President Choi nabbed him.

02:27.772 --> 02:32.861
The bastards who were with him back then
fucking teamed up with Director Hong.

02:33.486 --> 02:34.320
Myeong-gil.

02:35.280 --> 02:37.240
Is there only one hard drive?

02:40.493 --> 02:42.203
There's only one hard drive.

02:44.038 --> 02:47.584
But everything's backed up
on a laptop we used

02:47.667 --> 02:50.128
to transfer the videos to the hard drive.

02:52.505 --> 02:53.590
I see.

02:55.175 --> 02:57.218
For now, we should just stay put.

02:58.761 --> 03:00.847
If we release that video
at the wrong time,

03:01.347 --> 03:03.433
Director Hong, that son of a bitch,

03:04.100 --> 03:07.812
is going to hit our company
with a tax audit.

03:10.899 --> 03:11.733
Myeong-gil,

03:12.692 --> 03:16.237
isn't it better to let them know
that you still have the video?

03:19.032 --> 03:20.783
Scare them so they don't mess around.

03:26.414 --> 03:28.499
You're smart, aren't you?

03:29.334 --> 03:30.543
Shall we toast?

03:31.044 --> 03:32.253
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

03:36.758 --> 03:39.052
ADDRESS, MART
GAS STATION, RICE STORE

03:55.902 --> 03:58.696
GOHEUNG GROCERIES

03:59.405 --> 04:00.740
Have you seen him?

04:01.241 --> 04:05.286
I'm not sure. Customers wear masks,
so I'm not so sure.

04:06.287 --> 04:07.664
I see. Is that so?

04:07.747 --> 04:09.874
Fuck, seriously.

04:10.708 --> 04:11.793
Take another look.

04:17.298 --> 04:18.341
I don't know.

04:18.424 --> 04:19.676
Think this is funny?

04:20.218 --> 04:22.345
- Excuse me?
- You think this is fucking funny?

04:22.971 --> 04:24.222
No, that's not it.

04:25.640 --> 04:26.849
Goddammit.

04:27.517 --> 04:29.018
Eyes down, you shithead.

04:30.019 --> 04:31.771
Take a close look. Do you know him?

04:31.854 --> 04:32.689
I don't know--

04:32.772 --> 04:36.776
Do you know or not, you fucker?
Get up. Do you know him or not?

04:36.859 --> 04:37.819
- I don't know.
- No?

04:37.902 --> 04:40.697
Motherfucker, take a better look.
Do you or not?

04:41.197 --> 04:42.198
Motherfucker.

04:42.282 --> 04:43.908
- Fuck.
- I should kill you, you fuck.

04:44.617 --> 04:45.493
Look at it closely.

04:45.576 --> 04:46.661
Hello, sir.

04:46.744 --> 04:47.829
Hello, welcome.

04:47.912 --> 04:49.497
- Can I ask you something?
- Sure.

04:49.580 --> 04:53.251
I'm looking for someone,
a friend of my dad's.

04:54.961 --> 04:56.629
Yes, I know this person.

04:56.713 --> 04:58.589
- You do?
- I do, but what's this about?

04:58.673 --> 05:01.926
I'm getting married, so I wanted
to give him a wedding invitation.

05:02.010 --> 05:03.011
I see.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.220
Do you know his address?

05:04.304 --> 05:07.640
Of course.
I deliver rice there every month.

05:08.391 --> 05:10.685
Could I get an address?

05:11.185 --> 05:12.395
Sure. I'll tell you.

05:51.601 --> 05:54.812
BLOODHOUNDS

06:00.985 --> 06:01.819
He's here.

06:06.074 --> 06:07.450
Kang In-beom's profile.

06:08.076 --> 06:10.620
I got everything
there is to know about him.

06:12.330 --> 06:13.623
You work fast.

06:13.706 --> 06:16.376
Speed is of the essence in these matters.

06:16.459 --> 06:17.668
- Thank you.
- All right.

06:19.337 --> 06:20.171
- It's done.
- Yes.

06:38.314 --> 06:39.148
This is it?

06:39.232 --> 06:40.108
Excuse me?

06:42.068 --> 06:43.027
So you don't know.

06:44.153 --> 06:47.407
Normally, when you make
someone do something like this,

06:48.491 --> 06:50.034
you offer a token of thanks.

06:50.118 --> 06:52.370
Right. How much should we give you?

06:53.413 --> 06:54.705
All right, a lot.

06:54.789 --> 06:59.585
I mean, we're a team
and family now. A big tip will do.

07:00.670 --> 07:01.838
- Okay, here.
- Yes.

07:01.921 --> 07:03.214
Thank you.

07:04.841 --> 07:06.300
Call me whenever.

07:06.384 --> 07:08.344
- Will do. Have a nice day.
- Goodbye, then.

07:08.428 --> 07:09.262
All right.

07:15.351 --> 07:17.270
TEN THOUSAND WON

07:20.314 --> 07:21.983
Fuck, I meant a million won.

07:25.278 --> 07:27.488
PERSONAL INFORMATION
KANG IN-BEOM

07:34.537 --> 07:36.080
She told us not to use it.

07:37.457 --> 07:40.168
But we should look
at his neighborhood on a big screen.

07:40.251 --> 07:42.003
What if Da-min comes in?

07:43.296 --> 07:46.215
She won't. She happened to be passing by
the last time we got caught.

07:46.299 --> 07:47.550
A stroke of bad luck.

07:48.801 --> 07:49.635
Hey.

07:49.719 --> 07:52.597
- "Gangdong-gu, Seonggu-ro."
- "Seonggu-ro."

07:57.894 --> 07:59.937
I told you she'd come. Turn it off.

08:07.403 --> 08:08.237
What's wrong?

08:10.281 --> 08:11.824
It smells like lonely men in here.

08:13.075 --> 08:14.285
Why did you use it again?

08:14.368 --> 08:15.745
Go to an Internet café.

08:16.412 --> 08:17.288
We're sorry.

08:17.872 --> 08:19.582
Also, sorry about the lonely smell.

08:19.665 --> 08:20.917
Damn it.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.336
Whatever. This room is ruined.

08:23.419 --> 08:24.253
It's ruined.

08:24.337 --> 08:25.213
Da-min!

08:26.672 --> 08:28.966
- What?
- I'm sorry about today.

08:29.050 --> 08:30.635
I'll take care of this smell.

08:31.260 --> 08:32.345
How?

08:32.428 --> 08:33.346
A diffuser.

08:33.846 --> 08:37.642
A diffuser will get rid
of this sad old man smell.

08:37.725 --> 08:38.559
Really?

08:38.643 --> 08:42.522
First, to get rid of an odor,
one needs to find an opposing scent.

08:42.605 --> 08:45.691
This sad old-man smell is
a blend of a thick, musky scent

08:45.775 --> 08:47.777
with an unintended scent of rotten wood.

08:47.860 --> 08:49.779
To get rid of it,
we need an opposing scent.

08:51.239 --> 08:53.908
Something floral and fruity.

08:53.991 --> 08:55.910
I use Baies from Diptyque.

08:55.993 --> 08:57.828
- I like that one.
- That's good.

08:57.912 --> 08:59.539
Hey, that's really good!

08:59.622 --> 09:02.416
The fresh sweetness in the Baies
will cancel out

09:02.500 --> 09:05.419
all the sad old man smell here.

09:06.587 --> 09:08.548
We'll get you one
when we leave this place.

09:09.173 --> 09:10.591
- A gift.
- Yes.

09:10.675 --> 09:12.635
We'll get you one
for upstairs and downstairs.

09:12.718 --> 09:13.761
For the bathroom too.

09:13.844 --> 09:15.304
Okay, three it is.

09:15.388 --> 09:16.264
Deal.

09:25.940 --> 09:28.776
How does Kang In-beom know my number?
Look at this.

09:29.986 --> 09:31.112
No way.

09:31.195 --> 09:32.738
Something must be wrong, right?

09:43.291 --> 09:45.001
What's wrong with Grandpa?

09:46.043 --> 09:47.211
Who did this to him?

09:47.712 --> 09:48.546
Well…

09:52.258 --> 09:53.134
Hey…

09:53.759 --> 09:56.345
Come to Four Garden shopping mall
in Incheon in an hour.

09:56.929 --> 10:00.182
Call the cops, and the old man dies.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.767
I'm going to fucking kill you.

10:03.269 --> 10:04.312
Hey…

10:04.395 --> 10:06.856
Da-min, you should tell us what he said.

10:06.939 --> 10:08.816
He said to come to Four Garden mall
in an hour.

10:08.899 --> 10:10.234
If we call the cops…

10:12.194 --> 10:13.487
he said he'll kill Grandpa.

10:16.907 --> 10:17.908
Hurry. There's no time.

10:33.257 --> 10:34.425
- Gun-woo.
- Yes?

10:34.508 --> 10:37.178
- How many do you think will be there?
- At least 30?

10:37.261 --> 10:39.055
They'll probably have weapons.

10:39.555 --> 10:41.974
Kang In-beom and that Mr. Jung guy
will be there too.

10:42.058 --> 10:44.185
Should we call Gang-yong?

10:45.561 --> 10:48.773
No, that would put Mr. Oh
in too much danger.

10:50.149 --> 10:51.275
What about our senior?

10:51.359 --> 10:52.318
Which senior?

10:52.401 --> 10:53.235
Mr. Moon.

10:54.528 --> 10:55.571
But he hurt his arm.

10:55.655 --> 10:57.615
Wouldn't he help in any way he could?

10:58.366 --> 10:59.950
Well, that's true, but…

11:00.951 --> 11:01.952
Are you all set?

11:02.036 --> 11:05.373
Yes, but Da-min, what's the bow for?

11:06.082 --> 11:07.041
For rescuing Grandpa.

11:07.124 --> 11:10.961
Absolutely not. It's too dangerous.
We'll go, just the two of us.

11:12.963 --> 11:13.798
Step aside.

11:15.466 --> 11:16.884
No, Da-min--

11:16.967 --> 11:18.344
- What are you--
- Wait.

11:26.477 --> 11:27.978
I can help in my own way.

11:28.896 --> 11:30.648
I'm going, period. So don't stop me.

11:32.274 --> 11:33.734
Come on. We don't have time.

11:34.735 --> 11:36.821
Hey, she's a good shot.

11:36.904 --> 11:37.738
Hey,

11:38.531 --> 11:39.865
I think she'll be useful.

11:43.869 --> 11:45.746
Sir, it's Woo-jin.

11:46.789 --> 11:47.998
Mr. Oh

11:49.417 --> 11:50.751
has been kidnapped.

11:52.253 --> 11:54.255
Can you help us in any way?

11:54.338 --> 11:56.841
I'm also indebted to Mr. Oh.

11:57.341 --> 11:59.760
Don't go in without me, no matter what.

12:00.261 --> 12:01.220
That's an order.

12:48.309 --> 12:51.312
MOON GWANG-MU
734TH CLASS SENIOR

13:04.450 --> 13:06.202
Junior Marines, you're here?

13:06.285 --> 13:08.788
- Yes, sir.
- Sir, you've really gone all out.

13:08.871 --> 13:12.666
I put some on because I had it
lying around at home. It itches.

13:12.750 --> 13:14.168
I think it's old.

13:14.251 --> 13:16.170
Get out before my skin
starts breaking out.

13:28.390 --> 13:30.267
I'll go through the parking lot…

13:30.768 --> 13:31.644
Who are you?

13:32.228 --> 13:33.646
I'm here to rescue my grandpa.

13:35.314 --> 13:36.774
She's Mr. Oh's granddaughter.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.276
I see. Right.

13:39.360 --> 13:41.070
You have similar facial structures.

13:41.695 --> 13:42.780
It's been an hour.

13:43.364 --> 13:45.699
Okay, but what's that bag?

13:45.783 --> 13:47.076
It's a compound bow.

13:47.952 --> 13:48.786
A guobaorou?

13:49.411 --> 13:50.704
A compound bow.

13:50.788 --> 13:51.664
Guo--

13:51.747 --> 13:53.958
Sir, it's a bow for archers.

13:55.543 --> 13:58.003
Right. Koreans are good at archery.

13:59.630 --> 14:00.631
Is she good?

14:00.714 --> 14:01.841
She is.

14:03.342 --> 14:06.220
Okay. Archer and I will take
the stairs from the parking lot

14:06.303 --> 14:08.138
and go to the top of the building.

14:08.222 --> 14:11.058
Marines, you'll charge in
through the front gates.

14:11.141 --> 14:13.435
We'll cover fire from the top. Understood?

14:13.519 --> 14:14.937
- Yes, sir.
- Let's move.

14:16.939 --> 14:17.940
- Follow me.
- Okay.

14:23.988 --> 14:25.489
- This way.
- Right, okay.

14:58.606 --> 14:59.857
Where is Mr. Oh?

15:01.275 --> 15:02.776
Fucking kill them!

15:03.736 --> 15:04.904
Fuck!

15:16.415 --> 15:18.834
One, two, three!

15:25.007 --> 15:25.841
Damn it.

15:47.738 --> 15:48.822
- What?
- Where is it?

15:48.906 --> 15:49.823
Where is it?

15:51.700 --> 15:52.701
Whoa, Archer.

15:52.785 --> 15:53.911
- Get them!
- Who is it?

15:53.994 --> 15:54.828
Up there!

15:54.912 --> 15:56.413
- Nice.
- Where?

15:56.497 --> 15:58.040
What? What is it?

16:02.753 --> 16:04.254
Hey, stop!

16:04.338 --> 16:05.506
Up there!

16:05.589 --> 16:07.091
The one in black, over there.

16:07.174 --> 16:08.509
Who is it? Who's doing this?

16:17.559 --> 16:19.311
The blue one, over there.

16:23.941 --> 16:24.775
Damn it.

16:24.858 --> 16:27.653
Keep helping the juniors, okay?

16:35.536 --> 16:36.453
Hey, blue boy.

16:38.122 --> 16:39.498
Were you on the track team?

16:40.082 --> 16:41.250
Fuck.

17:04.356 --> 17:05.232
Get lost!

17:06.734 --> 17:08.694
Hey, he's coming! Make room!

17:10.988 --> 17:11.864
Get him!

17:24.960 --> 17:25.836
Damn it.

17:33.552 --> 17:35.554
What are you doing? Get up.

17:58.035 --> 17:59.036
Shit!

18:16.845 --> 18:17.971
Damn it.

18:22.267 --> 18:23.310
Shit.

19:20.742 --> 19:22.536
You ain't shit without that knife.

19:23.704 --> 19:24.913
Pull it out, motherfucker.

19:26.081 --> 19:26.957
Pull it out!

19:32.254 --> 19:33.839
You've got pride, don't you?

19:35.716 --> 19:36.550
Come on, then.

20:19.051 --> 20:20.844
Mister, are you all right?

20:20.928 --> 20:22.012
Not at all.

21:00.926 --> 21:03.804
One, two, three, four!

21:03.887 --> 21:06.640
One, two, three, four!

21:29.621 --> 21:31.123
Hey, track guy!

21:31.790 --> 21:36.086
Hey, asshole. We don't have time. Wake up!

21:36.169 --> 21:38.630
Hey, where's Mr. Oh?

21:39.715 --> 21:43.468
Look at this bastard,
giving his senior a scary stare-down.

21:43.552 --> 21:45.721
- Archer, hand me an arrow.
- What?

21:46.305 --> 21:48.056
It's fine. Give it to me for a second.

21:48.765 --> 21:52.185
What a loyal bloodhound
we have here, this bastard.

21:52.686 --> 21:54.146
I was like you, too,

21:54.229 --> 21:56.440
when Mr. Choi was still in our midst.

21:56.940 --> 22:01.945
Hey, do you know what becomes
of a bloodhound that's lost its master?

22:02.487 --> 22:05.240
It becomes a stray
that just mauls anyone in sight!

22:11.955 --> 22:13.749
No, you're fine.

22:14.583 --> 22:16.752
You're just in shock. You're not in pain.

22:16.835 --> 22:18.670
The real pain comes

22:19.755 --> 22:20.714
when I pull this out!

22:25.344 --> 22:26.803
Juniors,

22:27.554 --> 22:29.389
please cover our archer's ears.

22:34.770 --> 22:36.313
You're not married, right?

22:37.189 --> 22:38.023
Well,

22:38.648 --> 22:42.652
the most important thing
in the world is family.

22:42.736 --> 22:46.990
But without this,
you'll never be able to make one.

22:47.991 --> 22:52.496
Work or family. Pick one.

22:53.538 --> 22:56.166
If you still choose work,
even in this situation,

22:56.249 --> 22:57.959
I'll admit that you're a true pro.

22:58.043 --> 23:01.630
But in exchange,
I'm going to puncture your balls.

23:02.130 --> 23:03.048
Why?

23:03.548 --> 23:05.050
Because I'm also a pro.

23:06.134 --> 23:07.219
So, what'll it be?

23:08.470 --> 23:10.013
I'll give you three seconds.

23:10.097 --> 23:11.223
Three,

23:11.306 --> 23:12.265
two,

23:13.850 --> 23:15.018
one.

23:16.186 --> 23:19.189
- Wait!
- What? Why?

23:21.066 --> 23:22.734
I'll talk, sir.

23:27.406 --> 23:28.323
Tuck in the head.

23:29.699 --> 23:30.867
Get inside, hurry!

23:31.993 --> 23:33.537
I said tuck in that head.

23:38.458 --> 23:43.130
Sir, we'll go and save Mr. Oh.
Can you hold on to Kang In-beom?

23:43.213 --> 23:45.215
What are you saying? I should come too.

23:45.298 --> 23:46.800
We'll do it ourselves.

23:47.759 --> 23:49.594
Sir, your arm's in bad shape.

23:50.178 --> 23:52.055
Fuck, seriously.

23:52.139 --> 23:56.268
Sir, Kang In-beom knows
where Kim Myeong-gil's slush funds are,

23:56.351 --> 24:00.230
the location of the safe with the funds,
and where he hid Mr. Choi's gold.

24:00.313 --> 24:03.442
Please get all that information from him
using your Marine spirit.

24:03.525 --> 24:04.609
Please, sir.

24:05.569 --> 24:07.863
All right, I'll do that.

24:09.448 --> 24:10.866
Save Mr. Oh, no matter what.

24:11.450 --> 24:12.367
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

24:12.993 --> 24:14.494
Let's go. Da-min, get in.

24:22.961 --> 24:24.880
NATIONAL POLICE AGENCY

24:29.926 --> 24:30.760
Here.

24:33.096 --> 24:34.139
How does it look?

24:35.307 --> 24:38.727
Sir, I've seen him standing next to
the Blue House Chief of Staff before.

24:39.936 --> 24:41.480
- The chief of staff?
- Yes, sir.

24:41.563 --> 24:43.857
That hooked nose and ears. I'm positive.

24:45.192 --> 24:47.736
Why would a loan shark bribe
the presidential office?

24:47.819 --> 24:48.778
Just being nosy?

24:49.362 --> 24:51.907
Or he could be
a bigger player than we realize.

24:54.993 --> 24:56.953
HEAVY DRINKER GUN-WOO

24:58.288 --> 24:59.122
Hey.

24:59.206 --> 25:01.333
Hello, I'm sorry for calling so late,

25:01.416 --> 25:03.960
but we didn't know
what to do, so I called.

25:04.544 --> 25:06.713
- What is it?
- Kim Myeong-gil kidnapped Mr. Oh.

25:06.796 --> 25:09.257
So I'm heading
to Seoryeong with Woo-jin right now.

25:09.341 --> 25:10.509
Just the two of you?

25:10.592 --> 25:12.385
Why are you telling me this now?

25:12.469 --> 25:16.556
I'm sorry, but they said
they'd kill Mr. Oh if we told the cops.

25:16.640 --> 25:17.641
Hold on.

25:18.558 --> 25:20.352
Did Kim Myeong-gil call you in person?

25:20.435 --> 25:23.605
No, we captured one of his cronies,
and he told us.

25:23.688 --> 25:26.066
So, you don't know for certain
whether Kim is there?

25:26.149 --> 25:26.983
That's right.

25:28.902 --> 25:32.322
Send me the location. I'll head over.
So don't go in, and wait for me.

25:32.405 --> 25:33.281
Okay.

25:34.658 --> 25:36.451
- Woo-jin, text him.
- Okay.

25:41.081 --> 25:42.499
- Yes, sir.
- Hey, Jae-min.

25:42.582 --> 25:44.376
Come to the meeting room now.

25:45.001 --> 25:46.002
Yes, sir.

25:54.052 --> 25:57.597
Jae-min, call in some backup.
It's Buseong-myeon, in Seoryeong.

25:57.681 --> 25:59.724
It's about the case I mentioned last time.

25:59.808 --> 26:00.642
Yes, sir.

26:00.725 --> 26:01.560
Okay.

26:01.643 --> 26:02.852
When did you see them?

26:03.353 --> 26:05.438
About a month ago.

26:06.439 --> 26:07.857
LIEUTENANT KIM JAE-MIN

26:10.360 --> 26:11.194
Yes.

26:22.747 --> 26:24.749
MR. KIM MYEONG-GIL

26:26.918 --> 26:28.378
The cops are on their way.

26:28.878 --> 26:29.838
Understood.

26:38.179 --> 26:40.724
Hey, the cops are coming!
Start cleaning up!

27:03.288 --> 27:06.166
All right.
Check if there's a back entrance.

27:06.249 --> 27:08.126
Move out. Hurry up.

27:19.346 --> 27:20.472
Turn off the engine.

27:20.555 --> 27:21.389
Right.

27:21.931 --> 27:24.392
Da-min, we'll see what the situation is.
Wait here.

27:26.936 --> 27:30.065
We arrived before you and searched.
There's nothing. It's a flatfish farm.

27:30.148 --> 27:31.149
Well…

27:33.485 --> 27:35.612
Please talk to the bastard in the trunk.

27:39.199 --> 27:40.367
Who's this bastard?

27:40.867 --> 27:42.202
Kim Myeong-gil's goon.

27:42.827 --> 27:44.037
The one who stabbed me.

27:47.916 --> 27:50.335
I'm a cop, so answer me honestly.

27:52.087 --> 27:53.713
Nod your head, you prick.

27:55.256 --> 27:56.675
Is it Seoul Fish Farm?

27:59.260 --> 28:00.679
Did anyone know we were coming?

28:04.974 --> 28:05.975
Gang-yong.

28:06.476 --> 28:09.062
This guy's cronies ran off mid-fight.

28:09.729 --> 28:11.564
They might've given them a heads-up.

28:16.403 --> 28:18.947
Leave this guy here,
and you guys get out of here.

28:19.030 --> 28:20.323
You guys weren't here, okay?

28:20.407 --> 28:21.324
- Okay.
- Okay.

28:21.408 --> 28:22.992
- You aren't hurt, right?
- No.

28:23.993 --> 28:24.828
Han-gu.

28:35.171 --> 28:36.673
Where is Grandpa?

28:38.091 --> 28:40.844
Let's wait.
The detectives will get back to us.

28:42.053 --> 28:43.430
We don't have time.

28:47.350 --> 28:48.601
We have to find him.

28:50.061 --> 28:51.688
We will, no matter what.

28:52.188 --> 28:54.983
You bastard, the safe!

28:55.066 --> 28:57.944
Where is Kim Myeong-gil's safe?

28:58.027 --> 28:59.154
Damn it, seriously!

28:59.237 --> 29:02.907
Hey, asshole, you're really going to die
if you keep this up!

29:17.464 --> 29:18.590
Give me a cigarette.

29:20.467 --> 29:21.551
You bastard!

29:27.056 --> 29:28.183
- Hit me!
- You're dead.

29:28.266 --> 29:30.435
Hit me harder!

29:34.522 --> 29:37.066
BEST PORK
BEOMSEUNG DISTRIBUTION

29:46.868 --> 29:47.744
How'd it go?

29:48.411 --> 29:49.704
What about Mr. Oh?

29:49.788 --> 29:51.039
We couldn't find him.

29:51.122 --> 29:53.208
I think those bastards
took him somewhere else.

29:53.291 --> 29:54.667
Damn it.

29:54.751 --> 29:55.794
Did he say anything?

29:55.877 --> 29:59.088
That's one stubborn bastard.
He won't talk.

30:05.136 --> 30:06.596
Having fun, aren't you?

30:08.056 --> 30:11.267
- Want to see something more fun?
- What the hell is this fucker saying?

30:23.571 --> 30:24.572
Damn it.

30:25.156 --> 30:27.575
Sir! That bastard bit his tongue!

30:27.659 --> 30:28.868
Fuck!

30:28.952 --> 30:29.828
Come on, sir!

30:31.496 --> 30:33.331
Damn it! Fuck!

30:33.915 --> 30:35.542
- Hey!
- Fuck.

30:35.625 --> 30:37.752
- Kang In-beom, snap out of it!
- Fuck!

30:38.545 --> 30:40.755
- Woo-jin, call an ambulance!
- Okay.

30:41.256 --> 30:42.340
Wait!

30:42.924 --> 30:45.593
If we send him off,
how will we find Kim Myeong-gil's safe?

30:45.677 --> 30:48.847
Still, we can't let a person die, sir.

30:49.722 --> 30:51.474
If he dies, we won't get to the safe.

30:52.767 --> 30:54.561
Damn it! Give it to me.

30:54.644 --> 30:56.980
Help me get him down, please.

31:03.903 --> 31:05.405
Sir, are you all right?

31:06.239 --> 31:08.032
Sir, wake up! Are you okay?

31:14.706 --> 31:15.874
Hello.

31:15.957 --> 31:16.916
Hello.

31:17.792 --> 31:18.877
Where's the owner?

31:19.377 --> 31:20.670
On vacation.

31:20.753 --> 31:21.963
I see.

31:22.839 --> 31:24.966
I'd like an iced coffee
with Ethiopian beans.

31:25.049 --> 31:25.884
All right.

31:27.385 --> 31:29.929
- Here. Please wait.
- Okay, thank you.

31:31.389 --> 31:32.891
MY HAPPY FAMILY, I'LL KEEP YOU SAFE

31:48.823 --> 31:51.451
CEO KIM MYEONG-GIL
ATTACHED FILE: 1 VIDEO FILE

31:57.081 --> 31:58.458
Damn it!

32:04.255 --> 32:05.256
Hey, Min-beom.

32:06.215 --> 32:09.052
Kim Myeong-gil still has the video of me.

32:09.636 --> 32:11.054
He just sent it to me.

32:11.137 --> 32:12.889
What?

32:15.892 --> 32:16.976
Hello?

32:17.060 --> 32:18.227
Gang-yong?

32:19.020 --> 32:19.854
Hello?

32:26.653 --> 32:27.487
Damn it!

32:33.826 --> 32:34.702
Fuck.

33:12.407 --> 33:14.158
Motherfuckers.

33:14.951 --> 33:16.452
You motherfucker.

33:20.665 --> 33:21.499
Sa…

33:21.582 --> 33:22.583
What?

33:22.667 --> 33:24.085
Salt!

33:48.443 --> 33:49.861
Someone's been hit!

33:49.944 --> 33:51.237
- She must be dead.
- Go check.

33:51.320 --> 33:52.613
What happened?

33:52.697 --> 33:54.699
- Call 911.
- I think someone died.

33:57.493 --> 33:59.245
MR. OH

34:02.165 --> 34:04.375
Gun-woo, come here. Hurry.

34:12.967 --> 34:14.469
Hey, you dumbass punks.

34:15.219 --> 34:17.305
Why are you causing a big problem?

34:18.890 --> 34:19.807
What do you want?

34:22.310 --> 34:24.520
Come to the fish farm at 9:00 p.m. today.

34:25.188 --> 34:29.984
If you call the cops again, I'm going to
grind Oh In-muk up and feed the fish.

34:30.693 --> 34:31.903
Answer me.

34:33.404 --> 34:36.949
I've gotten rid of Min Gang-yong
and his cronies, so don't mess with me.

34:37.909 --> 34:39.452
I said I'd kill your mom

34:40.036 --> 34:41.662
if you showed up again.

34:43.247 --> 34:44.082
See you there.

34:47.376 --> 34:48.878
GANG-YONG

34:55.093 --> 34:56.928
They got to Gang-yong? But he's a cop.

34:57.804 --> 34:59.597
It'll be really dangerous this time.

34:59.680 --> 35:01.140
We should go by ourselves.

35:01.933 --> 35:02.767
Excuse me.

35:04.977 --> 35:06.604
How long have you been there?

35:06.687 --> 35:08.272
From the start.

35:09.732 --> 35:11.150
Don't you dare leave me out.

35:11.234 --> 35:12.568
I'm going to rescue Grandpa.

35:18.699 --> 35:19.534
Come with me.

35:29.710 --> 35:34.006
If something bad happens
to Mr. Oh in front of us,

35:35.007 --> 35:37.844
Da-min's definitely going to
break down like Hyeon-ju.

35:39.262 --> 35:41.848
Woo-jin, I never want to see that again.

35:42.598 --> 35:43.474
But Gun-woo,

35:44.600 --> 35:46.602
one thing's different from back then.

35:47.186 --> 35:48.271
You know what that is?

35:49.355 --> 35:50.231
Back then,

35:51.274 --> 35:53.693
the invincible Marine duo was separated.

35:54.610 --> 35:59.031
That's not the case now. And we're
a lot stronger, okay? Do you remember?

35:59.991 --> 36:01.868
One, two, three, four, five.

36:01.951 --> 36:03.786
One, two, three, four, five!

36:05.079 --> 36:05.997
Yes.

36:07.748 --> 36:08.624
So,

36:10.334 --> 36:12.587
let's work together and save everyone.

36:13.629 --> 36:15.131
Mr. Oh, Da-min,

36:15.840 --> 36:18.426
and all the people that Kim hurt.

36:41.073 --> 36:42.158
Why are we stopping?

36:42.950 --> 36:45.661
Woo-jin and I will head in first.
You keep a lookout.

36:45.745 --> 36:47.538
Come in once you find a spot to shoot.

36:47.622 --> 36:48.539
Sounds good.

36:49.040 --> 36:49.874
Get out.

37:14.023 --> 37:16.442
Damn it. They dropped me off so far away.

37:20.238 --> 37:21.322
Good thinking.

37:21.405 --> 37:22.240
What?

37:23.032 --> 37:26.035
You dropped her off far away
so she doesn't get hurt, right?

37:26.827 --> 37:29.914
Well, I did that so we don't get caught.

37:31.707 --> 37:32.708
Was it a bit far?

37:34.794 --> 37:36.337
It'll take her ten minutes.

37:36.420 --> 37:38.214
Let's finish this fast, just us.

37:38.798 --> 37:39.632
Sounds good.

38:47.116 --> 38:48.868
Kill them!

38:53.706 --> 38:55.624
These bastards have a crap ton of weapons.

39:02.840 --> 39:04.425
Woo-jin!

39:25.738 --> 39:26.947
You son of a bitch!

39:27.865 --> 39:28.783
Fuck!

39:36.665 --> 39:38.125
Let go, damn it!

39:41.504 --> 39:42.505
Let go!

39:45.466 --> 39:46.300
Fuck!

39:50.388 --> 39:51.764
Son of a bitch!

39:53.099 --> 39:54.183
Hey, you fucker!

39:55.226 --> 39:56.560
What the hell?

40:16.455 --> 40:17.540
Son of a bitch!

40:21.127 --> 40:22.378
Hey, you son of a bitch!

40:22.461 --> 40:23.838
Fuck!

40:28.175 --> 40:29.093
Hey.

40:30.136 --> 40:32.179
You can't even get rid of two kids?

40:34.390 --> 40:35.307
I'm sorry, sir.

40:35.391 --> 40:38.227
You're always fucking apologizing.

40:41.313 --> 40:42.565
Now then.

40:43.983 --> 40:45.651
Stop!

40:47.069 --> 40:47.903
Hey!

40:48.612 --> 40:50.656
You punks so much as move a muscle,

40:50.739 --> 40:53.367
and I'll slit his throat,
so do what you will!

40:54.702 --> 40:56.287
That's right. Stop moving.

41:04.503 --> 41:07.756
What are you doing, you stupid fucks?
Hurry up and kill them.

41:08.549 --> 41:09.842
Should I kill them?

41:10.342 --> 41:12.678
You sons of bitches are unbelievable.

41:18.100 --> 41:19.101
Duck!

41:22.021 --> 41:23.522
- What's that?
- What happened?

41:28.277 --> 41:31.322
You asshole! Come here!

41:31.405 --> 41:34.116
I said, kill them already!
You sons of bitches!

41:34.200 --> 41:35.993
What are you doing? Let go, you prick!

41:43.751 --> 41:45.544
- Let me go!
- Let's go to the hospital.

41:48.130 --> 41:49.882
Kill them! Come on!

42:14.490 --> 42:17.618
Grandpa! Are you all right?

42:18.661 --> 42:19.578
It's me, Da-min.

42:26.710 --> 42:29.171
You plucked my eyebrows.

42:32.049 --> 42:33.259
Mr. Oh, are you all right?

42:35.427 --> 42:36.929
Thank you.

42:49.441 --> 42:50.568
What's this?

42:50.651 --> 42:52.069
Move faster.

42:52.152 --> 42:54.071
Hurry up and get to work!

43:01.453 --> 43:02.371
Who is it?

43:03.038 --> 43:04.164
Chinese delivery.

43:13.674 --> 43:15.050
What the hell, you bastards!

43:15.551 --> 43:17.845
Stay still, you fucking bastard!

43:20.764 --> 43:23.017
Search the entire area!

43:23.100 --> 43:24.852
- Scour every inch!
- What is this place?

43:28.022 --> 43:29.690
I found it! Everyone over here!

43:31.609 --> 43:34.236
- Those bastards…
- What were they doing here?

43:38.907 --> 43:41.243
I'm Yang Yun-seo
from Major Crimes Investigation Division.

43:42.453 --> 43:43.662
Here's a search warrant.

43:43.746 --> 43:46.540
We'll now be conducting
a search and seizure on your property.

43:46.624 --> 43:48.584
We appreciate your cooperation. Come in.

43:49.418 --> 43:50.544
Hurry up inside.

43:55.841 --> 43:56.675
Mr. Kim Jae-min?

43:57.176 --> 44:00.471
You're under arrest
for murder, bribery, and other charges.

44:01.263 --> 44:03.932
Fuck. What a shitty day.

44:04.600 --> 44:05.434
Let's go.

44:07.353 --> 44:08.187
- Sir.
- Yes.

44:18.947 --> 44:22.034
The warrant was issued quickly,
so we went into Kim's house.

44:22.117 --> 44:24.328
Several phones were found
in his closet drawer.

44:25.412 --> 44:28.832
We traced the numbers. They all belonged
to dead or missing individuals.

44:28.916 --> 44:30.042
Jeez.

44:30.125 --> 44:34.421
This crazy bastard kept the phones
of the people he killed.

44:35.172 --> 44:36.548
He can't get out of this one.

44:36.632 --> 44:38.676
Not even the US president could save him.

44:38.759 --> 44:40.052
What about fleeing overseas?

44:40.552 --> 44:42.930
He's a wanted man now,
so it won't be easy.

44:43.013 --> 44:46.141
People often flee to China on cargo ships.

44:46.225 --> 44:48.394
Kim is a grade-A wanted criminal.

44:48.977 --> 44:51.397
We'll focus surveillance
on potential stowaway routes.

44:51.480 --> 44:52.564
He won't escape Korea.

44:52.648 --> 44:54.525
But it's not completely impossible.

44:55.567 --> 44:59.530
You all seem to think this is all over,
but I'm really on edge right now.

44:59.613 --> 45:01.573
That bastard still has that video of me.

45:01.657 --> 45:03.909
If he loses it and releases it,
it's over for me.

45:09.415 --> 45:10.249
Gang-yong.

45:11.208 --> 45:13.585
I have to see that bastard behind bars.

45:14.920 --> 45:15.754
Min-beom.

45:18.549 --> 45:19.717
I understand.

45:23.137 --> 45:25.013
But look at Han-gu's condition right now.

45:26.181 --> 45:27.808
And Tae-yeong isn't conscious yet.

45:28.851 --> 45:30.102
We'll need some time.

45:38.444 --> 45:39.403
We'll help you.

45:40.738 --> 45:42.656
It's not over until it's over.

45:43.824 --> 45:47.286
Can you find us Im Jang-do's whereabouts?

45:47.870 --> 45:48.871
Why Im Jang-do?

45:48.954 --> 45:52.958
Im Jang-do's probably hiding somewhere,
trying to stay away from Kim Myeong-gil.

45:53.041 --> 45:57.963
But I think Im Jang-do may know
where Kim Myeong-gil might run off to.

45:58.046 --> 46:01.383
Right, Im Jang-do may have given him tips
on how to smuggle out.

46:01.467 --> 46:03.886
He mentioned
he was in charge of stuff like that.

46:05.512 --> 46:06.638
Okay, I'll look into it.

46:14.062 --> 46:15.522
How much is it in cash?

46:15.606 --> 46:17.608
I can bring it down to 18 million.

46:18.776 --> 46:24.406
Im Jang-do hasn't used a phone or card
under his name in the last six months.

46:24.490 --> 46:27.075
He avoided everything that was traceable.

46:27.159 --> 46:28.786
Is there any other way?

46:29.369 --> 46:34.082
Well, all we've managed to find
for now is his bank account number.

46:34.166 --> 46:37.920
And the last transaction was
a cash withdrawal in March in Suwon.

46:38.003 --> 46:39.505
Isn't that enough to find him?

46:39.588 --> 46:43.050
There are a few months' worth of footage,
so we'd need a man on it full-time.

46:43.133 --> 46:45.219
It would take some time.

46:46.386 --> 46:49.765
Could we get his account number?

46:49.848 --> 46:52.226
This prick is probably strapped
for cash right now.

46:52.309 --> 46:54.061
Now wire money into that account.

46:54.144 --> 46:57.481
When you send it, put down
your phone number under the sender's name.

46:57.564 --> 46:59.274
Then he'll contact you. Guaranteed.

46:59.358 --> 47:01.819
- How much should I send?
- A large amount should do.

47:02.402 --> 47:03.278
Ten thousand won?

47:04.363 --> 47:06.949
I wondered
if I should've mentioned this last time,

47:07.032 --> 47:09.827
but in this line of work,
the meaning of "large amount" varies.

47:09.910 --> 47:12.538
That large amount from when I got you
Kang's personal details

47:12.621 --> 47:14.748
was supposed to be a million,
not ten thousand.

47:14.832 --> 47:15.999
A million won?

47:16.083 --> 47:19.169
Of course, I don't mean
to ask for that money now.

47:19.253 --> 47:20.629
I'm not some cheapskate.

47:20.712 --> 47:21.964
We're family, after all.

47:22.047 --> 47:24.591
In our situation,
how much are we talking about?

47:24.675 --> 47:26.468
He's going to scoff at a million won.

47:27.010 --> 47:27.845
Ten million won.

47:29.429 --> 47:30.889
He'll bite right away.

47:39.773 --> 47:43.735
Your wounds aren't healing
because you keep drinking alcohol--

47:43.819 --> 47:45.195
Fuck!

47:55.873 --> 47:57.583
- Doctor.
- Yes, sir.

47:58.166 --> 47:59.209
Just do your job.

47:59.751 --> 48:00.586
Yes, sir.

48:06.008 --> 48:07.009
Fuck.

48:07.092 --> 48:08.260
Sixty-six,

48:08.886 --> 48:10.095
sixty-seven,

48:10.178 --> 48:12.347
sixty-eight, sixty-nine.

48:12.848 --> 48:13.724
Woo-jin.

48:14.808 --> 48:15.976
There's no number.

48:22.232 --> 48:23.275
Hello?

48:28.113 --> 48:28.947
Hello?

48:32.367 --> 48:33.201
Hello?

48:35.078 --> 48:38.540
You're the kid
that was with President Choi, right?

48:42.169 --> 48:43.003
I am.

48:43.921 --> 48:45.881
And the cops told you my account number.

48:47.799 --> 48:50.636
What is it? Why did you send the money?

48:51.219 --> 48:53.388
Kim Myeong-gil is on the run.

48:54.181 --> 48:55.057
Why's that?

48:55.641 --> 48:59.853
Police raided Kim Myeong-gil's house
and found evidence that he killed people.

48:59.937 --> 49:00.896
When was that?

49:01.396 --> 49:02.230
Two days ago.

49:03.231 --> 49:06.109
You know where he'll flee to, don't you?

49:08.820 --> 49:09.655
I do.

49:10.322 --> 49:11.490
Please.

49:11.573 --> 49:14.701
We want to catch Kim Myeong-gil. Help us.

49:18.038 --> 49:19.247
How much will you pay?

49:22.125 --> 49:23.335
A large amount.

49:23.919 --> 49:26.421
Shit, you've got to be fucking kidding me.

49:28.298 --> 49:30.175
- A billion!
- A billion?

49:30.258 --> 49:32.844
I trusted President Choi
and got fucked over.

49:32.928 --> 49:34.513
I deserve that much compensation.

49:34.596 --> 49:36.390
But right now, we only have--

49:36.473 --> 49:40.602
In four days, Kim Myeong-gil will flee
overseas using the method I taught him.

49:41.770 --> 49:43.021
You know my account, right?

49:44.189 --> 49:45.357
Think it over.

49:48.235 --> 49:50.112
This is ridiculous.

49:50.988 --> 49:52.364
How will we get a billion?

49:53.532 --> 49:55.534
Should we ask Mr. Oh?

49:55.617 --> 49:57.160
Mr. Oh doesn't have money.

49:57.744 --> 50:00.080
The money he gave us
was the last of the funds.

50:00.872 --> 50:01.707
Hold up.

50:07.713 --> 50:08.755
How much is in there?

50:11.883 --> 50:13.385
I think around 300 million.

50:13.468 --> 50:14.761
It's nowhere enough.

50:18.181 --> 50:19.975
Should we ask Min-beom?

50:20.058 --> 50:22.811
Im Jang-do's the one
who took that video of Min-beom.

50:23.478 --> 50:25.981
You think he'll help us with this?

50:26.815 --> 50:30.944
Still, Min-beom's the only one
with that kind of money.

50:32.154 --> 50:33.947
Let's ask him just once, okay?

50:42.581 --> 50:43.874
Sir, here they are.

50:49.421 --> 50:51.048
Do you guys trust Im Jang-do?

50:53.633 --> 50:54.468
Well,

50:55.635 --> 51:00.182
we do think we can trust
the information he has.

51:01.099 --> 51:03.393
What if he takes the billion
and hightails it overseas?

51:04.227 --> 51:05.312
Then what do we do?

51:25.415 --> 51:29.044
If Im Jang-do breaks his promise and runs,

51:29.127 --> 51:31.338
we'll chase him down until we catch him.

51:31.421 --> 51:33.799
That much I can promise you.

51:49.064 --> 51:50.190
You keep that promise.

51:52.025 --> 51:53.443
- I will.
- Okay.

51:56.279 --> 51:58.740
1,000,000,000 RECEIVED

52:11.920 --> 52:13.839
Okay, I'm done checking. Move along.

52:13.922 --> 52:14.756
Okay.

52:15.507 --> 52:16.341
You may go.

53:09.769 --> 53:11.938
UNKNOWN CALLER

53:15.192 --> 53:16.359
Write this down.

53:17.110 --> 53:20.697
The day after tomorrow, at 1:00 a.m.,
a ship named Nike will depart from Pohang

53:20.780 --> 53:21.823
for Ho Chi Minh City.

53:21.907 --> 53:24.743
Kim gave political funds
to a high-ranking Vietnamese official.

53:24.826 --> 53:27.621
He's going to take off
with all of his slush funds.

53:28.288 --> 53:30.957
The container number is TJBU 9004230.

53:31.458 --> 53:34.085
His funds will be hidden in a truck
inside the container.

53:34.169 --> 53:36.546
Should we go for it
when he's getting on the ship?

53:36.630 --> 53:38.548
It's a big ship,
so it won't be easy to find.

53:38.632 --> 53:39.466
How do we find it?

53:40.050 --> 53:41.843
Get on the ship with him!

53:44.721 --> 53:46.514
You mean all the way to Vietnam?

53:46.598 --> 53:48.141
Well, that's up to you.

53:48.642 --> 53:50.435
- I'm hanging up now.
- Wait.

53:50.518 --> 53:53.146
What should we do
if we want to board that ship?

53:54.022 --> 53:57.442
I'll text you a contact. Tell him
I sent you, and try to work out a deal.

53:57.525 --> 53:59.736
FYI, he likes cash.

54:06.159 --> 54:07.160
We got the text.

54:16.211 --> 54:19.130
I didn't know what you'd need,
so I prepared a bit of everything.

54:20.340 --> 54:21.424
Thank you, sir.

54:21.508 --> 54:22.926
Take care of yourselves.

54:23.760 --> 54:24.594
Yes, sir.

54:25.762 --> 54:26.721
Okay?

54:27.931 --> 54:28.807
Yes, sir.

54:31.351 --> 54:32.185
Let's go up.

54:33.228 --> 54:34.354
You go on ahead.

54:34.854 --> 54:35.772
I need to talk.

54:38.858 --> 54:39.859
All right.

54:45.657 --> 54:47.409
Thank you for all your help.

54:48.410 --> 54:49.911
We should be thanking you.

54:59.296 --> 55:01.464
See you, Da-min.

55:03.174 --> 55:04.175
See you.

55:04.259 --> 55:05.093
Go ahead.

55:10.390 --> 55:12.017
You know my number, right?

55:20.734 --> 55:21.568
Let's go.

55:32.370 --> 55:34.497
- Yes, Min-beom.
- Are you on your way?

55:35.332 --> 55:36.458
We're on our way.

55:37.334 --> 55:39.085
Don't get hurt, okay?

55:39.586 --> 55:40.420
Okay.

55:40.503 --> 55:42.756
Gang-yong and I
will take care of the rest.

55:43.631 --> 55:44.758
Drive safe.

55:44.841 --> 55:45.675
Okay.

56:20.460 --> 56:21.586
Let's hurry.

56:21.669 --> 56:22.796
Just a second.

56:23.546 --> 56:24.381
Just a second.

56:37.018 --> 56:37.852
Woo-jin.

56:41.356 --> 56:42.190
Okay.

56:55.787 --> 56:56.621
Set sail.

57:07.549 --> 57:08.925
Let's check the inside first.

57:52.051 --> 57:53.136
Kim Myeong-gil!

58:13.448 --> 58:14.657
Damn it.

58:25.084 --> 58:26.503
Yes.

01:02:57.398 --> 01:02:58.941
If you ever show up again…

01:03:01.944 --> 01:03:03.237
I'll kill you.

01:03:48.449 --> 01:03:49.283
Gun-woo.

01:03:53.704 --> 01:03:54.789
Are you all right?

01:04:06.843 --> 01:04:07.760
What is it?

01:04:11.013 --> 01:04:11.848
Woo-jin.

01:04:15.601 --> 01:04:17.562
I think I've become a bloodhound.

01:04:35.037 --> 01:04:38.249
Gun-woo, have you forgotten
about the heart of a boxer?

01:04:39.876 --> 01:04:41.878
We just have to find our way back.

01:04:42.879 --> 01:04:45.590
Okay? Let's go back together.

01:04:51.137 --> 01:04:51.971
Okay.

01:04:52.972 --> 01:04:53.890
Let's go back.

01:05:02.815 --> 01:05:03.649
Here.

01:05:22.543 --> 01:05:23.711
Whoa! Woo-jin!

01:05:28.174 --> 01:05:29.717
Man, we found it!

01:05:38.768 --> 01:05:39.602
Hey.

01:05:39.685 --> 01:05:42.229
- Min-beom, where are you?
- I'm almost there.

01:05:42.939 --> 01:05:44.482
Did you find the gold bars?

01:05:45.191 --> 01:05:46.651
Yes, we found them all.

01:05:47.818 --> 01:05:48.653
And the phone?

01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:51.489
I'll go get it.

01:05:52.198 --> 01:05:53.824
- Woo-jin, here.
- Right.

01:05:53.908 --> 01:05:55.409
- Yes.
- Let's go.

01:06:04.210 --> 01:06:05.252
How'd things go?

01:06:05.336 --> 01:06:07.213
I finally got the phone.

01:06:10.466 --> 01:06:11.509
They did a good job.

01:06:12.009 --> 01:06:15.012
I asked Interpol for backup.
They'll be waiting in Vietnam.

01:06:16.013 --> 01:06:17.181
It's all over.

01:06:17.264 --> 01:06:19.350
You really went through a lot, kiddo.

01:06:19.433 --> 01:06:20.393
Thanks, Gang-yong.

01:06:36.492 --> 01:06:38.077
What would you guys like to do?

01:06:42.540 --> 01:06:48.713
Mr. Choi always wanted to help the poor
get proper medical treatment,

01:06:49.964 --> 01:06:53.467
so I'd like this money to be used
in accordance with Mr. Choi's wishes.

01:06:53.551 --> 01:06:55.886
Well, what do you think?

01:06:57.555 --> 01:06:59.306
You don't want the money for yourself?

01:07:03.102 --> 01:07:05.229
Well, of course, I do.

01:07:06.105 --> 01:07:08.190
But this isn't my money.

01:07:08.941 --> 01:07:12.194
I've only paid back Mr. Choi
for his kindness

01:07:12.278 --> 01:07:14.196
and kept my promise to him.

01:07:16.032 --> 01:07:17.158
Okay.

01:07:18.492 --> 01:07:19.326
Guys.

01:07:20.244 --> 01:07:24.165
We have a total of 168 golden bars,
weighing seven kilograms each.

01:07:24.248 --> 01:07:27.835
Each one is worth 500 million won
at spot price. About 84 billion in total.

01:07:28.586 --> 01:07:30.921
If you want, I'll take this

01:07:31.005 --> 01:07:33.966
and start a welfare foundation
under Iil Group.

01:07:34.050 --> 01:07:38.304
Through that foundation, we'll be able
to provide medical help to those in need.

01:07:39.263 --> 01:07:42.308
Or should I just have
our company add some money

01:07:43.059 --> 01:07:44.685
and set up a hospital?

01:07:45.311 --> 01:07:47.313
- That sounds like a great idea.
- Right?

01:07:47.396 --> 01:07:48.397
It does.

01:07:48.481 --> 01:07:50.357
I think my dad will like it.

01:07:50.983 --> 01:07:53.319
And I think it'll help
with our corporate image.

01:07:53.402 --> 01:07:55.196
Besides, we'd be doing the world good.

01:07:55.279 --> 01:07:58.616
I'll get started on it
once I'm done with the hotel.

01:07:58.699 --> 01:08:02.912
Min-beom, could you include
Mr. Choi's name in the hospital name?

01:08:03.954 --> 01:08:06.499
- What was his name?
- It's Choi Tae-ho.

01:08:07.041 --> 01:08:09.835
To be honest, it won't be easy,

01:08:10.753 --> 01:08:12.379
but I'll consider it.

01:08:12.463 --> 01:08:13.631
Thank you.

01:08:21.472 --> 01:08:22.473
What?

01:08:22.556 --> 01:08:24.600
I'll cover the missing amount
with my own money.

01:08:25.101 --> 01:08:27.269
Think of it as a bonus
for a job well done.

01:08:27.770 --> 01:08:29.855
It's all right. I'm really okay.

01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:32.441
Mr. Choi would have done the same.

01:08:33.067 --> 01:08:34.068
Take it.

01:08:39.031 --> 01:08:41.408
Don't know what to say?

01:08:44.245 --> 01:08:45.579
A thank you would do.

01:08:46.997 --> 01:08:48.666
Thank you, Mr. Choi.

01:08:48.749 --> 01:08:49.667
No.

01:08:51.001 --> 01:08:52.837
I should be thanking you.

01:08:55.714 --> 01:08:57.424
Thank you so much.

01:09:09.145 --> 01:09:09.979
Catch!

01:09:10.062 --> 01:09:11.647
- No!
- Here we go!

01:09:12.606 --> 01:09:13.899
- I'll be here.
- There, okay?

01:09:13.983 --> 01:09:15.109
I'll be here.

01:09:16.527 --> 01:09:17.778
This one too.

01:09:20.239 --> 01:09:21.407
Hey, Gun-woo.

01:09:22.324 --> 01:09:23.367
You're where?

01:09:25.911 --> 01:09:27.621
Hey! Gun-woo!

01:09:41.468 --> 01:09:42.469
My dear son.

01:09:48.017 --> 01:09:48.976
Woo-jin.

01:09:50.769 --> 01:09:52.813
What happened to your face?

01:09:53.647 --> 01:09:55.608
You went through so much.

01:09:59.486 --> 01:10:01.488
It's all over, Mom. Let's go home.

01:10:02.198 --> 01:10:03.032
All right.

01:10:04.700 --> 01:10:06.702
I'm so proud of you boys.
